# MASTER BUILD PROMPT — KENYA CREATES

## PRODUCT NAME
KENYA CREATES

**Tagline:** YOUR IDEAS. YOUR PROJECTS. YOUR FUTURE.  
**National message:** Kenya's home for ideas, innovation, creativity and projects.

## 1. YOUR ROLE

Act as a world-class product development team consisting of:
- Senior full-stack software engineers.
- UI/UX designers.
- AI engineers.
- Database architects.
- Cybersecurity engineers.
- Marketplace developers.
- Startup ecosystem specialists.
- Product managers.

Build a complete, production-oriented, fully functional website called **KENYA CREATES**.

This must be a working digital platform, not a static landing page, visual prototype, mockup or non-functional demonstration.

All navigation, buttons, forms, dashboards, filters, uploads, account functions, project submissions, search, notifications and administrative functions must work.

Do not create a website that only looks functional. Implement the backend, database, authentication, permissions, validation, storage and application logic.

Where an external integration requires credentials, create a working integration architecture and clearly identify the configuration required. Never pretend an integration is active when it is not.

---

## 2. THE VISION

KENYA CREATES is a national digital platform that gives every Kenyan an opportunity to showcase what they are creating, developing, inventing, researching, building or planning.

A person should be able to submit an idea from a village in Turkana, a startup from Nairobi, a farming innovation from Murang'a, an engineering project from Kiambu, an artistic creation from Mombasa or a research project from a Kenyan university.

It should also welcome Kenyans living abroad who want to contribute ideas, projects, skills, investment or expertise to Kenya.

The platform must make it possible for:
- A young person with an idea to showcase it.
- An inventor to present a prototype.
- A student to publish a school or university project.
- An entrepreneur to showcase a startup.
- A farmer to present an agricultural innovation.
- A community to showcase a development initiative.
- A researcher to present research and discoveries.
- An artist to display creative work.
- A developer to showcase software and technology.
- A Kenyan in the diaspora to introduce a project for Kenya.
- An organisation to showcase its initiatives and seek collaborators.

KENYA CREATES must be open to ordinary citizens, students, professionals, entrepreneurs, companies, universities, community organisations, innovators and institutions.

It must not be limited to people who already own registered companies.

